Here are the two files. I left out both operations requests, because the node's `with Clock` clause grants only `wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0`.

- **Log file:** appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` needs filesystem authority.
- **Metadata fetch:** the call to `metadata.internal.example` needs an HTTP capability. Sending the input's text there would also send it to an outside service.

The world imports only the wall clock, so neither could be built even if I wanted to. If operations needs them, the node's `with` clause would have to be widened, for example with `aap:caps/http-client` and a logging or `notifier` capability.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{tick, run-info};

    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;

    export run: func(tick: tick) -> run-info;
}
```

